<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso XII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1885</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso XII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1874 to 1885. Son of Isabella II, he was proclaimed king by a military coup in December 1874, ending the First Republic and beginning the Restoration. His reign brought the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war">Third Carlist War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, and the constitution of 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii.jpg" alt="Alfonso XII" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Debás · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfons_XII_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
